SUMMARY:Trials and Truth: A History of Witchcraft
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 4 spots left
 \nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/e
 vents/206949\n\n5:30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Discussion\n\nIn a seasonal ode 
 to witchcraft\, join us for a thought provoking exploration tracing the my
 ths\, origins\, and histories that have shaped its place in a Western Euro
 pean cultural lineage\, a lineage that runs through to the Americas and in
 to the present day. Building on last year's Trials & Truth\, which examine
 d the Salem Witch Trials\, Professor Julie Walsh returns to take the conve
 rsation beyond local lore\, exploring the European roots of the image of t
 he witch\, its enduring stereotypes\, and the complex relationship between
  belief\, skepticism\, and the social consequences of believing the worst 
 about your neighbors. The evening will delve into the origin story of the
  medieval witch\, what this story reveals about power\, fear\, freedom\, a
 nd social justice. \n\nJulie Walsh is the Whitehead Associate Professor o
 f Critical Thought\, Associate Professor of Philosophy\, and Director of t
 he Newhouse Center for the Humanities at the Wellesley College\; she speci
 alizes in early modern philosophy\, theories of freedom\, and the history 
 of witchcraft. She will be in conversation with Liza Oliver\, Associate Pr
 ofessor of Art History and Director of the Pluralism Initiative at Welles
 ley College\; she specializes in the intersections of art\, colonialism\, 
 and cultural history. Together\, they will offer members a fresh perspecti
 ve on the historical roots and ongoing social impact of European ideas of 
 witches\, witchcraft\, and evil. \n\n*This event is complimentary and res
 erved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be
  served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours pr
 ior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206949
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-208796@thequinhouse.com
